    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>O2 model of the article: <strong>Selective oxidation of 3-hydroxypropionic acid to malonic acid over Pd/C: Mechanistic and kinetic study.</strong> Kim S.Y., Chavarrio J., Install J., Huber G.W. <i>Appl. Catal. B: Environ. Energy</i> 386 (2026) 126403. DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403">10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403</a></p>
        <p>Conditions: 60 mM 3-HP, 0.2 g 10 % Pd/C, NaOH/3-HP = 1:1, 3 bar O2, 50 C (Fig. 9b). Rate constants: Table 3 (O2 column) as printed. Six first-order irreversible steps; the reaction orders and equilibrium constants of SI Table S4 are not used. </p>
        <p>Inferred from the authors&apos; data deposit (Dryad, DOI 10.5061/dryad.jsxksn0q4), not stated in the paper: the oxidant reference factor x_O2_ref = 15*0.000339 on reactions 1, 2 and 4, and the use of the depleting O2 activity state yO2. </p>
        <p>NSKinetics addition: the Arrhenius temperature dependence k(T) of the six steps (paper Eq. 6 form, T_ref = 50 C), with activation energies from the paper text and from the authors&apos; heat-map script. The paper&apos;s own heat maps (Fig. 11) and the 25/75/100 C curves (Fig. 10) were computed with a different, simplified reversible five-reaction model (not this file); away from 50 C this file is an extrapolation that the paper does not show. </p>
      </body>
